  "question": {
    "text": "If $I_1=\\int_0^1 e^{-x} \\cos ^2 x d x ; I_2=\\int_0^1 e^{-x^2} \\cos ^2 x d x$ and $I_3=\\int_0^1 e^{-x^3} d x$; then",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "PdHEA",
      "text": "\n$I_2>I_3>I_1$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ZyMCk",
      "text": "\n$I_3>I_1>I_2$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "6z0yc",
      "text": "\n$I_2>I_1>I_3$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "z5Uma",
      "text": "\n$I_3>I_2>I_1$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given:\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&I_1=\\int_0^1 e^{-x} \\cos ^2 x d x \\\\\n&I_2=\\int_0^1 e^{-x^2} \\cos ^2 x d x \\text { and } \\\\\n&I_3=\\int_0^1 e^{-x^3} d x \\\\\n&\\text { For } x \\in(0,1) \\\\\n&\\Rightarrow x>x^2 \\text { or }-x < -x^2 \\\\\n&\\text { and } x^2>x^3 \\text { or }-x^2 < -x^3 \\\\\n&\\therefore e^{-x^2} < e^{-x^3} \\text { and } e^{-x} < e^{-x^2} \\\\\n&\\Rightarrow e^{-x} < e^{-x^2} < e^{-x^3} \\\\\n&\\Rightarrow e^{-x^3}>e^{-x^2}>e^{-x} \\\\\n&\\Rightarrow I_3>I_2>I_1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
